"""Private-key fixtures, stored base64-encoded and written out at test time.

Committing real PEM private-key blocks to a repository trips
secret-scanning push protection on GitHub and every other host, and trains
reviewers to wave private keys through. These are throwaway keys generated only
to exercise the DER/OpenSSH parsers, so they are kept base64-encoded here and
materialized into ``tmp_path`` by :func:`materialize` when a test needs them.

Public material (certificates, ``*.pub``, DH parameters) IS committed as real
files next to this module — it is not secret, and it lets the repo dogfood
PQC015/PQC016 in CI.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

